#### 3. Execution Flow in [vaayu_base.py](file:///c:/laragon/www/Vaayu/vaayu/vaayu_base.py)
When `generate` calls `self.speculator.draft(generated, past_key_values, num_tokens=self.draft_tokens)`:
- If `PromptLookupDecoder` is active, it runs the tensor-based sliding window match on the CPU/GPU instantly, returning the next matching slice from `generated`.
- The main engine streams the prompt/context layers from NVMe to VRAM. When running verification, it evaluates the base model on `verify_input = torch.cat([generated[:, -1:], draft_ids], dim=1)`.
- If 4 tokens match, Vaayu updates the active position index and cuts out 4 NVMe streaming cycles!
- Since `PromptLookupDecoder.rollback_cache` is a no-op, there is no state tracking or secondary model cache memory synchronization required.

